#: src/gui/about.rs:49
msgid ""
"Each time it starts, Ferret looks for a new version and downloads it. It's "
"installed when you press Restart or the next time Ferret starts. Turned off, "
"Ferret never looks by itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/gui/about.rs:57
msgid ""
"New versions come when Flatpak or your software centre updates your apps. "
"Turned off, Ferret stays on this version until you install one here."
msgstr ""

#: src/gui/about.rs:65
msgid ""
"To change a game's numbers, Ferret reads and writes the memory of the game "
"you pick, through a small helper program with the same rights as you. So a "
"bug or a bad update could reach your files, not only the game. It refuses "
"games with anti-cheat and online-only games. Ferret isn't signed with a "
"certificate, so Windows may warn about an unknown publisher, and an "
"antivirus may flag the helper, because some malware changes other programs' "
"memory too."
msgstr ""

#: src/gui/about.rs:76
msgid ""
"To change a game's numbers, Ferret reads and writes the memory of the game "
"you pick, through a small helper program that runs outside Flatpak's sandbox "
"with the same rights as you. So the sandbox doesn't protect you from Ferret: "
"a bug or a bad update could reach your files, not only the game. It refuses "
"games with anti-cheat and online-only games. On some systems it asks for "
"your password so the helper may open games, and the helper keeps only that "
"one permission."
msgstr ""

